<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Louis I, Duke of Bavaria</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1173">1173</a>–<a href="/years/1231">1231</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a> · Also known as Louis the Kelheimer</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Louis I, called the Kelheimer, was Duke of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bavaria">Bavaria</a> of the house of Wittelsbach from 1183 to 1231. In 1214 Emperor Frederick II granted him the Palatinate of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rhine">Rhine</a>, which his family secured by marrying his son Otto II to the Welf heiress Agnes, beginning nearly six centuries of Wittelsbach rule there. He founded towns such as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/landshut">Landshut</a> and was murdered on the bridge at Kelheim in 1231.</p></div>
